    - JSON.stringify floating-point precision (elapsed_effective_seconds is a float; Godot's JSON outputs as a float; round-trip equality — test asserts with tolerance or exact? Godot's JSON.stringify(float) uses the shortest round-trip representation… risk of precision drift; the test asserts with strict comparison of the restored float (round-trip should be exact; if not, record and clamp to tolerance in GDScript float64? The float values here are sums of binary-precise ticks; stringify→parse round-trip should preserve double). Note as risk R: JSON float round-trip; test asserts equivalence and documents failure.
    - user:// under isolated HOME: runner isolates HOME; tests additionally use explicit temp dir.
    - Backup semantics: keep a single .bak (last good), no unbounded backups.
    - Rollback: all changes in Phase B are new files under scripts/save/** + tests/**; schema and example are single-file edits — rollback = git revert of the commit, or file deletion; no data migration of existing user saves (v0.1 unreleased, no real user saves; the v1 path exists only for tests).
    - Scope discipline: no UI, no EventLog file (LOG-001), no economy parameters, no GameController changes — integration is deferred to a later ticket (UI-001/LOG-001). The plan must make this explicit as an interface gap: "GameController currently doesn't wire SaveService; within Phase B scope we don't modify scripts/core/**; the save load/save orchestration is first implemented and acceptance-tested in AtomicSaveService + test assembly, then wired into GameController in the UI-001 ticket (or listed as a gap in review)."

