One consideration — is this ticket a candidate for BLOCKED? Does it involve a requirements change / breaking operation / high-risk decision? The v1→v2 migration refusal policy could be called a "save compatibility" decision — per AGENTS.md, the user retains final approval authority over save compatibility. But per REQUIREMENTS_CHANGELOG/DEV_LOG, the project owner has already delegated auto-approval to Codex for the local v0.1 tickets ("明确允许 Codex 自动审批、处理问题并完成项目，无需逐票询问 (explicitly permit Codex to auto-approve, handle issues, and complete the project without per-ticket inquiries)"), and the queue has needs_human=false, and the ticket explicitly requires Phase A to "propose a plan" for the migration policy ("必须提出...安全处置 (must propose a...safe handling)"), and says "若计划认为还需修改其他运行时模块，先指出接口缺口并在独立审查中决定 (if the plan believes other runtime modules also need changes, first point out the interface gaps and let independent review decide)" — i.e., the workflow routes decisions to independent review, not to a human. My plan doesn't change requirements; it proposes a fail-closed, non-destructive design within the allowed scope. The migration refusal policy is a design choice within the ticket's explicit instructions (the ticket itself mandates a safe handling: "必须安全拒绝并保留原档或仅迁移可证明安全的状态 (must safely refuse and retain the original file, or only migrate provably-safe state)"). So no BLOCKED needed; finish with PHASE-A-DONE.

