Is this ticket in a state where it needs to be blocked? Let me think through it: the ticket mentions a high-risk decision (a save migration policy that rejects v1 saves containing processed transactions). The brief itself pre-approved this: "Must propose a v1→new-version migration with no silent loss; clearly define the safe handling method for cases where a v1-processed transaction has no fingerprint ledger; fabricating idempotent data is not allowed" — this is explicitly asking me to propose such a policy within the plan, and the AUTO-001 flow has an independent plan review before Phase B (the brief says "Phase B's candidate scope is… if the plan determines that other runtime modules must also be changed, first point out the interface gap and decide in independent review. Do not overstep on your own"). The plan stays within the allowed file scope (no changes to other modules; gaps G-1..G-4 are flagged for review, not implemented). The v1 rejection policy is fail-closed and non-destructive (preserves the original file; there are no actual user saves for v0.1). It does not change economic parameters, does not change the UI, does not change the SDD product scope, and does not do any git writes. Therefore, this is not a BLOCKED condition — Phase B will be gated by the independent review as per the established AUTO-001 process. AGENTS.md §6 requires owner approval for "destructive save migration" — the plan explicitly avoids destructive migration (rejects + preserves; no destructive transformation of existing saves is executed whatsoever). Also, the owner's delegation on record (REQUIREMENTS_CHANGELOG 2026-11-11: Codex auto-approval, no need to ask for each ticket individually) covers the Phase B approval for this local v0.1 ticket within scope, as demonstrated by FSM-001/ECO-001. So end with PHASE-A-DONE.
